Author: M.Takeuchi <46990346+MasayukiTa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 27 11:34:28 2026 +0900

    Accept version-4 transfer records on the receive path
    
    * Accept v4 transfer records on the production receive path
    
    open_signed_record and the DHT fetch/local-record checks in node.rs now decode with decode_record_value_any, so a version-4 record is opened and validated instead of being refused. A v3 record decodes byte for byte as before. A v4 record is accepted but its manifest is not yet threaded through the v3 receive engine, so it rides as None pending a follow-up.
    
    * Add receive-side tests for v4 transfer records
    
    Cover open_signed_record: a v4 record opens, a v3 record still opens with its manifest unchanged, and a truncated, hostile-version, or length-mismatched v4 trailer is refused without a panic. The size limit still applies to a v4 manifest.

